comments.body:
Could we drop `DynSock::Wait()` entirely instead? The base `Sock::Wait()` already handles this without taking ownership of the socket, and `DynSock::WaitMany()` always returns `true`, so the behavior should remain unchanged.

Leaving this to the base `Sock` implementation might also make things simpler for anyone working in this area in the future.

If you agree, perhaps something like this would work:

<details>
